# KISS Engineering Principle

When implementing or changing code in this repository:

- Prefer the simplest design that solves the requirement.
- Minimize code lines and moving parts.
- Avoid adding abstractions unless they are clearly necessary now.
- Keep interfaces narrow: small inputs/outputs, minimal configuration surface.
- Favor straightforward control flow over clever patterns.
- Refactor toward less complexity when touching nearby code.

If two solutions are viable, choose the one that is easier to explain, test, and maintain.
